## Summary Matrix

| # | Area                          | Impact    | Effort       | Priority |
|---|-------------------------------|-----------|--------------|----------|
| 1 | Operator cognitive load       | High      | Quick win    | P1       |
| 2 | Task formulation burden       | Medium    | Moderate     | P2       |
| 3 | Output readability            | Med-High  | Moderate     | P2       |
| 4 | Escalation experience         | High      | Moderate     | P1       |
| 5 | Role understanding/onboarding | Medium    | Quick win    | P2       |
| 6 | Progress visibility           | Medium    | Quick win    | P3       |
| 7 | Language barrier/translations | Med-High  | Moderate     | P2       |
| 8 | Feedback loop                 | Medium    | Quick win    | P3       |

---

## Recommended Implementation Order

**Iteration 1 (quick wins, low risk):** Items 1, 5, 6, 8 — templates and conventions only, no protocol changes. Can be implemented concurrently.

**Iteration 2 (moderate, requires doc coordination):** Items 2, 3, 4 — introduces new structural elements across `protocol-core.md` and `fallback-mode.md`. Should be sequenced because they touch related sections (phase definitions, artifact formats).

**Iteration 3 (ongoing maintenance):** Item 7 — translation quality controls become part of the operating rhythm, not a one-time change. Best introduced after Iteration 1 establishes a feedback habit.

